.TH GIT-PRCHUM 1 "2026-08-28" "prchum 0.5.0" "Git Extensions"
.SH NAME
git-prchum \- review a git comparison in prchum
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B git prchum
.RI [ options ]
.RI [ target ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Opens
.BR prchum (1)
on a comparison in the current repository. git runs any
.B git\-*
on the PATH as a subcommand, so this is reachable as
.BR "git prchum" .
.PP
It changes to the repository's top level before starting, so
.B git prchum
in a subdirectory shows the whole comparison, matching how other git
commands behave.
.PP
Arguments are
.BR prchum (1)'s.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-\-staged ", " \-\-cached
Compare the index against HEAD.
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
.B git prchum
The working tree against HEAD.
.TP
.B git prchum \-\-staged
The index against HEAD.
.TP
.B git prchum main
This branch against main.
.TP
.B git prchum v1..v2
A range.
.SH CONFIGURATION
An alias makes it the command you type:
.PP
.RS
.EX
git config \-\-global alias.d '!git prchum'
.EE
.RE
.SH EXIT STATUS
Non\-zero outside a git repository, or when
.BR prchum (1)
cannot read the comparison.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR prchum (1),
.BR git\-diff (1)
.SH AUTHOR
Horacio Duran
